.TH ORO-INTERNAL-TCP-SOCKET 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:internal/tcp\-socket \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:internal/tcp\-socket'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
oro:internal/tcp\-socket is a JavaScript API module exposed by the Oro Runtime.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBTCPSocket\fR
This is an exported `ClassDeclaration` named `TCPSocket`, but it does not yet have a dedicated description in the generated reference.
.TP
\fBconstructor(remoteAddress, remotePort, options)\fR
Notes \- Gating: if disabled by policy, `opened` rejects immediately and no underlying socket is created. \- 'opened' resolution: deferred until native emits 'connect'; errors before that reject `opened`. \- Readable semantics: enqueues Uint8Array; closes on 'end'. \- Writable semantics: resolves per\-write callback; backpressure is handled by the underlying socket and surfaced via the callback.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIremoteAddress\fR (string; required) Hostname or IP.
.br
\fIremotePort\fR (number; required) Destination port (0..65535).
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TCPSocketOptions; optional)
.TP
\fBopened()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBclosed()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
